<section id="capability-papers" aria-labelledby="papers-heading">
  <div class="papers-heading"><div><span>CAPABILITY PAPERS</span><h2 id="papers-heading">Two decisions. Evidence you can inspect.</h2></div><p>Read the derivation, inspect the checks, or change the inputs and generate your own report.</p></div>
  <div class="papers-grid">
    <article><div class="paper-type">01 / FLOW · LIVE OPENFOAM</div><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper.pdf" aria-label="Read the channel pressure-loss paper"><img src="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/paper-preview.png" alt="Computed and analytical pressure losses for three channel gaps against the pressure budget" width="900" height="450" loading="lazy"/></a><h3>Which channel gap meets the pressure budget?</h3><p>Nine solves. Three grids per gap. Reference, conservation and residual checks.</p><strong>Changed-input proof: 2.5 mm is the smallest passing tested gap.</strong><div class="paper-actions"><a class="paper-primary" href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper.pdf">Read PDF paper ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/current/?study=channel">Change inputs →</a><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper-sources.zip">LaTeX + evidence ↓</a></div><small>25 mL/s · 40 Pa budget · idealized parallel-plate flow. Not hardware validation.</small></article>
    <article><div class="paper-type">02 / THERMAL · ANALYTICAL SCREENING</div><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper.pdf" aria-label="Read the forced-convection cooling-channel paper"><img src="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/paper-preview.png" alt="Temperature versus pumping-pressure trade for three cooling-channel layouts" width="900" height="450" loading="lazy"/></a><h3>Which cooling layout meets both budgets?</h3><p>Energy balance. Three layouts. Adverse scenarios and a radial heat-transfer verification.</p><strong>Worked screen: two 2 mm passages pass the stated thermal and friction limits.</strong><div class="paper-actions"><a class="paper-primary" href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper.pdf">Read PDF paper ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/cooling/">Change inputs →</a><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper-sources.zip">LaTeX + evidence ↓</a></div><small>100 W · 72 °C inner-wall limit · 2 kPa straight-channel budget. No thermal CFD claimed.</small></article>
  </div><p class="paper-note">Research-style technical reports, not peer-reviewed publications. Each states what its calculations establish—and what still needs validation.</p>
  <p class="paper-note"><strong>Structural extension · Rev 1.0</strong> Bracket, pressure tube and thermal restraint: 21 CalculiX solves, with failed and incomplete gates retained. <a href="/software/aero/current/?case=fea-bracket-20260912">Explore in Aero →</a> · <a href="/demos/aero/fea-v1/README.html">Read the acceptance report →</a></p>
</section>
